{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLClefV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLClef","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","title":"MXLClef","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLClef","kind":"identifier"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clefs are represented by a combination of sign, line, and clef-octave-change elements. The optional number"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute refers to staff numbers within the part. A value of 1 is assumed if not present."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Content-swift.struct"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/init(id:content:number:isAdditional:size:isAfterBarline:position:font:color:printsObject:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/color","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/content-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/font","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/id","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/isAdditional","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/isAfterBarline","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/number","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/position","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/printsObject","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/size"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Enumerations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Sign"],"anchor":"Enumerations"},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlclef"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLClef","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sometimes clefs are added to the staff in non-standard line positions, either to indicate cue passages, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when there are multiple clefs present simultaneously on one staff. In this situation, the additional attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is set to “yes” and the line value is ignored. The size attribute is used for clefs where the additional"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is “yes”. It is typically used to indicate cue clefs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sometimes clefs at the start of a measure need to appear after the barline rather than before, as for cues or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for use after a repeated section. The after-barline attribute is set to “yes” in this situation. The attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is ignored for mid-measure clefs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Clefs appear at the start of each system unless the print-object attribute has been set to “no” or the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"additional attribute has been set to “yes”."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"code":"<clef>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLClef/size":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The size of the clef, used when "},{"code":"additional","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", typically to indicate cue clefs."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/size","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlclef\/size","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"size","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLSymbolSizeO","text":"MXLSymbolSize","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"size","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLClef/font":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vs. a music font."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/Iv